index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..45ae91016083f9d4e129b0fe61347f0a3b53de63
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/oj-portfolio-bridge.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# OJ portfolio template import
+
+This downstream OJ-only feature is requested by the WordPress plugin operator.
+It does not change the upstream project format or local-only training model.
+
+The authenticated same-origin parent may append assignment questions only after
+an explicit student click. The app advertises the current project ID and an
+ephemeral project token; both must match at mutation time. Opening, closing, or
+replacing a project invalidates the token. No project is created automatically.
+
+Incoming messages retain protocol-v2 source, origin, frame nonce, assignment,
+and storage-session binding. Request IDs correlate replies and make duplicate
+delivery idempotent. The existing append-only import function preserves answers
+and attachments. An existing question ID with different text is rejected instead
+of silently pairing an old answer with a new question.
+
+The app checks resource bounds, updates the existing project, waits for local
+storage, and then acknowledges. A storage failure retains the in-memory answers
+and reports failure; it never reports an unsaved import as success. A project
+switch or revocation prevents navigation and a stale success response. The
+parent keeps Markdown download/manual import as its fallback.
+
+Protocol fields and bounds are in frontend/src/oj-host-v2.ts,
+frontend/src/oj-portfolio-template.ts, and frontend/src/limits.ts.
